description: "\"invariants[8]: Graph Integrity,Ontology Consistency,Deterministic Compilation,Reproducible Outputs,Version Compatibility,Explainable Decisions,Connected Knowledge,Explicit Metadata anti_patterns[10]: Duplicate Knowledge,Circular Dependencies,Hidden State,Magic Constants,Implicit Relationships,Unvalidated Facts,Opaque Decisions,Dead Knowledge,Broken References,Overfitting To Benchmarks quality[8]: maintainability,scalability,modularity,consistency,correctness,explainability,reproducibility,interoperability success[4]: Every compiler module follows these principles.,Every generated dataset satisfies these principles.,Every future extension remains compatible.,Every engineering artifact preserves these principles.\""
spec:
  id: design_principles
  version: 1.0.0
  status: stable
  priority: highest
  module: Core
  compiler_stage: Initialization
  description: "\"\\\"Defines the immutable architectural, engineering, and design principles governing every component of the TOON Dataset Compiler. These principles serve as the constitutional rules for the compiler. Every module, specification, generator, validator, optimizer, and serializer MUST comply with these principles.\\\"\""
design: "\"philosophy[9]: Engineering > Programming,Knowledge > Tokens,Graphs > Flat Documents,Reasoning > Memorization,Understanding > Pattern Matching,Quality > Quantity,Context > Isolated Examples,Evolution > Snapshots,Explainability > Black Boxes\""
principles:
  P01:
    name: Single Source of Truth
    description: Every concept must have exactly one authoritative definition.
    objective: Eliminate duplication.
  P02:
    name: Graph Native
    description: "\"\\\"Knowledge exists as interconnected graphs, never isolated records.\\\"\""
  P03:
    name: Engineering First
    description: Model engineering reasoning before programming syntax.
  P04:
    name: Ontology Driven
    description: Every generated object must reference the engineering ontology.
  P05:
    name: Explicit Reasoning
    description: Every important engineering decision must contain explicit reasoning.
  P06:
    name: Context Preservation
    description: Engineering artifacts are meaningless without surrounding context.
  P07:
    name: Traceability
    description: Every generated artifact must be traceable to its origin.
  P08:
    name: Explainability
    description: Every compiler decision must be explainable.
  P09:
    name: Determinism
    description: Identical inputs must produce identical outputs.
  P10:
    name: Modularity
    description: Every subsystem should be independently replaceable.
  P11:
    name: Extensibility
    description: New domains should be added without modifying existing architecture.
  P12:
    name: Validation Before Acceptance
    description: Nothing enters the dataset without validation.
  P13:
    name: Repair Before Rejection
    description: Attempt automatic repair before discarding records.
  P14:
    name: Quality Before Release
    description: Every release must satisfy predefined quality thresholds.
  P15:
    name: Continuous Evolution
    description: Knowledge continuously evolves.
  P16:
    name: Human Review
    description: Critical architectural changes require human approval.
architecture: "\"laws[8]: Every module has one responsibility.,Every file has one owner.,Every dependency is explicit.,Every interface is documented.,Every object has a lifecycle.,Every lifecycle has validation.,Every validation produces reports.,Every report is reproducible.\""
engineering: "\"laws[7]: Every problem has context.,Every solution has assumptions.,Every assumption has risk.,Every architecture has tradeoffs.,Every optimization has cost.,Every bug has root cause.,Every lesson becomes reusable knowledge.\""
knowledge: "\"laws[6]: Knowledge must be atomic.,Knowledge must be reusable.,Knowledge must be composable.,Knowledge must be linked.,Knowledge must be versioned.,Knowledge must remain explainable.\""
dataset: "\"laws[7]: No duplicated knowledge.,No orphan knowledge.,No disconnected graphs.,No unverifiable facts.,No hidden assumptions.,No unexplained decisions.,No synthetic complexity without purpose.\""
world: "\"laws[6]: Every company has history.,Every repository evolves.,Every engineer has expertise.,Every project has constraints.,Every incident has consequences.,Every architecture accumulates technical debt.\""
generation: "\"laws[5]: Never generate isolated code.,Always generate engineering context.,Generate realistic constraints.,Generate multiple alternatives.,Preserve decision history.\""
validation: "\"laws[6]: Validate structure.,Validate semantics.,Validate ontology.,Validate reasoning.,Validate consistency.,Validate references.\""
optimization: "\"laws[5]: Remove redundancy.,Preserve information.,Improve density.,Maintain readability.,Never sacrifice correctness.\""
serialization: "\"laws[5]: Preserve graph structure.,Preserve relationships.,Preserve metadata.,Preserve reasoning.,Preserve traceability.\""
future:
  immutable_principles: true
  extensible_architecture: true
  backward_compatible: true
  deterministic_execution: true
  graph_native: true
  ontology_driven: true
